sentences.text:
Therefore, the following:
ORDER (i) The writ petition is allowed;
(ii) The impugned order dated 21.12.2018 passed by respondent No.2 vide Annexure-C is hereby set aside and quashed;
(iii) The matter is remitted back to the respondents for reconsideration afresh, in accordance with law and by directing the respondents to consider and dispose of the application filed by the petitioners under Section 28A of the Land Acquisition Act,
1894, without reference to the earlier application filed by the petitioners under Section 18 of the Land Acquisition Act, 1894, as expeditiously as possible, within NC:
2025:KHC:34244 HC-KAR a period of six months from the date of receipt of a copy Sri. Kempaiah Since Dead By Lrs., ... vs State Of Karnataka on 2 September, 2025

